Pin the dm-verity salt instead of generating one per build

The root hash is a function of (data, salt). Generating the salt with
uuidgen means the root hash changes on every build even when the
filesystem is byte-identical, so a user comparing the number on the
device against a published release compares two unrelated numbers.

Nothing about the output looks wrong, which is what makes it dangerous
rather than merely inconvenient: the tier 1 story rests entirely on that
number being comparable.

Also widens the salt to the full 32 bytes veritysetup takes. uuidgen
produces 16, and while libcryptsetup handles the short value the same
way every time, a value this project publishes should be the whole one.

Falls back to the previous behaviour when the variable is unset, so this
patch does not break a build that has not been told about it. That is
deliberate: a patch that made unrelated builds fail would be a patch
nobody upstream would take.

--- a/image/gpt/ab_userdata/pre-image.sh
+++ b/image/gpt/ab_userdata/pre-image.sh
@@
+# A pinned salt, when the caller supplies one. The root hash is a function of
+# (data, salt), so a salt that changes per build makes the root hash change per
+# build even when the filesystem is byte-identical.
+VERITY_SALT="${NULLROUTE_VERITY_SALT:-$(uuidgen | tr -d '-')}"
+
 VERITY_ARGS_SYSTEM="\
  --data-block-size ${IGconf_linux_page_size:-4096} \
  --hash-block-size ${IGconf_linux_page_size:-4096} \
  --hash sha256 \
  --uuid ${VERITY_UUID} \
- --salt $(uuidgen | tr -d '-') \
+ --salt ${VERITY_SALT} \
  --root-hash-file ${IGconf_image_outputdir}/system.roothash"
